# (name, year, when, region, lane, verdict, claim, truth, evidence, wiki)
H=[
("Operation Paperclip",1945,"1945–1959","USA and Germany","Global","Documented fact","The US secretly recruited Nazi scientists after World War II.","Over 1,600 German scientists, engineers and technicians were brought to the US, many with Nazi Party or SS membership, their records sanitised to avoid immigration rules. Wernher von Braun, who built the V-2 with slave labour, led NASA's Saturn V programme; Hubertus Strughold, linked to human experiments at Dachau, became a 'father of space medicine'. The USSR ran a similar programme (Operation Osoaviakhim).","Declassified US government files; the 1998 Nazi War Crimes Disclosure Act released many records.","Operation_Paperclip"),
("Unit 731 and the US cover-up",1936,"1936–1945, cover-up after 1945","Manchuria, China","East Asia","Documented fact","Japan ran a secret biological-weapons unit that experimented on humans, and its leaders escaped trial.","Unit 731 near Harbin, led by Shirō Ishii, performed vivisections, frostbite tests and deliberate infections with plague, anthrax and cholera on thousands of prisoners, mostly Chinese, and spread plague over Chinese cities, killing perhaps hundreds of thousands. After the war the US granted Ishii and his staff immunity in exchange for their data; several later held prominent medical posts in Japan.","Testimony at the Soviet Khabarovsk trials (1949); declassified US documents; Japanese researchers' confessions in the 1990s.","Unit_731"),
("MKUltra",1953,"1953–1973","USA and Canada","Global","Documented fact","The CIA secretly drugged people with LSD in mind-control experiments.","Under MKUltra, the CIA funded experiments at universities, hospitals and prisons, giving LSD and other drugs to people, sometimes without consent, and testing hypnosis and sensory deprivation; in Montreal, psychiatrist Ewen Cameron 'depatterned' patients with electroshock. CIA director Richard Helms ordered most files destroyed in 1973.","The 1975 Church Committee and 1977 Senate hearings, based on 20,000 surviving documents found in financial records.","MKUltra"),
("Tuskegee syphilis study",1932,"1932–1972","Alabama, USA","Americas","Documented fact","US health officials deliberately left Black men with syphilis untreated to study the disease.","The US Public Health Service followed about 600 poor Black men, 399 with syphilis, telling them they were treated for 'bad blood'. Even after penicillin became the standard cure in 1947, they were denied treatment. Dozens died and wives and children were infected. A whistle-blower, Peter Buxtun, leaked it to the press in 1972. President Clinton apologised in 1997. A related US study deliberately infected Guatemalans in 1946–48.","Associated Press report (1972); government investigations.","Tuskegee_Syphilis_Study"),
("Gulf of Tonkin incident",1964,"August 1964","Vietnam","Southeast Asia","Partly true","The second North Vietnamese attack used to justify US war in Vietnam never happened.","On 2 August 1964 North Vietnamese boats did attack the USS Maddox. But the reported second attack on 4 August almost certainly did not occur — sonar and radar misreadings in a storm. President Johnson used it to pass the Gulf of Tonkin Resolution, escalating the Vietnam War, in which over 3 million people died.","NSA historian Robert Hanyok's study, declassified in 2005.","Gulf_of_Tonkin_incident"),
("Operation Northwoods",1962,"1962","USA","Americas","Documented fact (proposed, rejected)","US military chiefs proposed staging fake terrorist attacks to justify invading Cuba.","The Joint Chiefs of Staff proposed staging attacks on US targets, including blowing up a ship at Guantánamo and faking the downing of a civilian plane, blaming Cuba. President Kennedy's administration rejected it.","Declassified in 1997 by the Assassination Records Review Board.","Operation_Northwoods"),
("Operation Legacy",1950,"1950s–1970s","British Empire","Global","Documented fact","Britain destroyed or hid colonial records before independence to cover up abuses.","As colonies became independent, British officials burned or dumped at sea records that might embarrass the government, including evidence of torture in Kenya's Mau Mau camps. Thousands of files were secretly kept in a Foreign Office archive at Hanslope Park until revealed during a 2011 court case by Kenyan victims, who won compensation in 2013.","The 'migrated archives' revealed in 2011.","Operation_Legacy"),
("Radium Girls",1917,"1917–1938","USA","Americas","Documented fact","Companies knew radium paint was poisoning women workers and hid it.","Young women painting watch dials with glow-in-the-dark radium paint were told to lick their brushes to a point. Many developed bone decay ('radium jaw'), anaemia and cancer. Company executives handled radium with protection, while doctors hired by companies blamed syphilis. The women's lawsuits (1928) helped establish workplace safety laws.","Court records; Kate Moore's history The Radium Girls.","Radium_Girls"),
("Leaded petrol cover-up",1923,"1923–2021","Global","Global","Documented fact","The industry promoted leaded petrol despite knowing lead was poisonous.","General Motors chemist Thomas Midgley developed tetraethyl lead in 1921; workers at plants died of lead poisoning, and Midgley himself was poisoned. Industry-funded scientist Robert Kehoe claimed for decades it was safe, until Clair Patterson's research proved widespread lead pollution. Lead exposure lowered IQ of hundreds of millions of children. The last country stopped selling it in 2021.","Historical records, scientific studies.","Tetraethyllead"),
("Tobacco industry cover-up",1953,"1953–1998","USA","Global","Documented fact","Tobacco companies knew smoking caused cancer and addiction but denied it.","Internal documents show companies knew by the 1950s–60s of the links to cancer and nicotine addiction, yet funded doubt and marketing. Lawsuits led to the 1998 Master Settlement Agreement.","The 'Tobacco Papers', millions of internal documents released in the 1990s.","Tobacco_Master_Settlement_Agreement"),
("COINTELPRO",1956,"1956–1971","USA","Americas","Documented fact","The FBI secretly spied on and sabotaged civil rights and political groups.","The FBI's counterintelligence programme infiltrated and disrupted groups including the Black Panthers and the civil rights movement; it sent Martin Luther King Jr. an anonymous letter urging him to kill himself. Activists who broke into an FBI office in 1971 exposed it.","Media, Pennsylvania FBI office documents; Church Committee.","COINTELPRO"),
("Watergate",1972,"1972–1974","USA","Americas","Documented fact","President Nixon's team burgled opponents and covered it up.","Men linked to Nixon's re-election campaign were caught breaking into the Democratic headquarters. Secret White House tapes revealed Nixon obstructed justice; he resigned in 1974.","Washington Post reporting, Senate hearings, White House tapes.","Watergate_scandal"),
("Iraq WMD intelligence",2002,"2002–2003","Iraq","Middle East","Documented fact","The case for the 2003 invasion of Iraq rested on false claims of weapons of mass destruction.","The US and UK claimed Iraq had active WMD programmes. No such weapons were found; key claims came from an unreliable source codenamed 'Curveball' and a plagiarised dossier. The war killed hundreds of thousands.","Iraq Survey Group (2004); UK Chilcot Inquiry (2016).","Iraq_and_weapons_of_mass_destruction"),
("NSA mass surveillance",2013,"revealed 2013","Global","Global","Documented fact","Governments secretly collected the phone and internet data of millions of ordinary people.","Edward Snowden, an NSA contractor, leaked documents showing programmes like PRISM collected data from tech companies, and allies including Britain's GCHQ tapped internet cables.","Snowden documents published by The Guardian and Washington Post.","Global_surveillance_disclosures_(2013%E2%80%93present)"),
("Smallpox blankets",1763,"1763","North America","Americas","Partly true","The British deliberately gave smallpox-infected blankets to Native Americans.","During Pontiac's War, British officers at Fort Pitt gave Delaware envoys blankets from a smallpox hospital, recorded in a trader's journal, and General Jeffery Amherst wrote approving the idea. Whether it caused an epidemic is unclear, as smallpox was already spreading. Most Native deaths from disease were not deliberate.","Letters of Amherst and Bouquet; William Trent's journal.","Siege_of_Fort_Pitt"),
("Holodomor cover-up",1933,"1932–1933","Ukraine","Europe","Documented fact","The Soviet Union hid a famine killing millions, aided by Western journalists.","The New York Times correspondent Walter Duranty denied the famine and won a Pulitzer Prize; Welsh journalist Gareth Jones, who reported it, was discredited and later murdered in Manchuria in 1935.","Soviet archives opened after 1991.","Holodomor"),
("Churchill and the Bengal famine",1943,"1943","Bengal, India","South Asia","Disputed and debated","Churchill's government made the Bengal famine worse.","About 3 million died. The war cabinet refused repeated requests to divert grain shipments, while India exported rice; Churchill made racist remarks about Indians. Some historians argue wartime shipping shortages limited options and that local hoarding and policy failures were also to blame. Both sides agree British policy failed catastrophically.","War cabinet records; Madhusree Mukerjee, Churchill's Secret War (2010); debates among historians.","Bengal_famine_of_1943"),
("Death of Subhas Chandra Bose",1945,"18 August 1945","Taiwan","South Asia","Unresolved","Bose did not die in the 1945 plane crash.","Japanese and Indian inquiries (Shah Nawaz Committee 1956, Khosla Commission 1970) concluded he died after a crash at Taihoku. The Mukherjee Commission (2005) said he did not die in the crash, but the government rejected its report. Theories that he lived as 'Gumnami Baba' in Faizabad were rejected by the Sahai Commission (2022). Ashes at Renkoji Temple, Tokyo, have never been DNA tested.","Commission reports; declassified Bose files (2016).","Death_of_Subhas_Chandra_Bose"),
("Death of Lal Bahadur Shastri",1966,"11 January 1966","Tashkent, USSR","South Asia","Unresolved","India's Prime Minister was poisoned in Tashkent.","Shastri died hours after signing the Tashkent Declaration. Officially it was a heart attack; no post-mortem was done in India, his body reportedly turned bluish, and his family raised questions. Key witnesses (his doctor and servant) died in accidents before testifying to a parliamentary committee in 1977. No evidence of poisoning has been proven.","Raj Narain Committee; RTI requests.","Lal_Bahadur_Shastri"),
("JFK assassination",1963,"22 November 1963","Dallas, USA","Americas","Disputed","Lee Harvey Oswald did not act alone.","The Warren Commission (1964) concluded Oswald acted alone. The House Select Committee (1979) said there was 'probably' a conspiracy based on acoustic evidence later discredited. Released files show the CIA hid information about its contacts with Oswald, fuelling suspicion, but no conclusive evidence of another gunman exists.","Warren Report; HSCA; JFK Records Act releases.","Assassination_of_John_F._Kennedy"),
("Reichstag fire",1933,"27 February 1933","Berlin","Europe","Disputed","The Nazis set the fire themselves to seize power.","Dutch communist Marinus van der Lubbe was arrested and executed. Hitler used the fire to suspend civil liberties. Historians debate whether van der Lubbe acted alone or Nazis were involved; either way it was the pretext for dictatorship.","Trial records; historians' research.","Reichstag_fire"),
("Tesla's seized papers",1943,"1943","New York","Americas","Documented fact (myth exaggerated)","The government seized Tesla's secret 'death ray' plans when he died.","When Tesla died in January 1943, the Office of Alien Property took his belongings, and an MIT engineer, John Trump, examined his papers for the FBI, concluding they were speculative with no secret weapon. Most papers later went to the Tesla Museum in Belgrade. The secret super-weapon story is unproven.","FBI files released under FOIA.","Nikola_Tesla"),
("Edison stole Tesla's inventions",1884,"1880s–1890s","USA","Americas","Mostly myth","Edison stole Tesla's work and cheated him.","Tesla claimed Edison promised $50,000 for improving dynamos and then joked he did not understand American humour. Edison did fight AC with fear campaigns. But AC patents were Tesla's own and sold to Westinghouse; Edison did not steal them. Many Edison 'inventions' were developed by employees.","Biographies; Tesla's autobiography.","War_of_the_currents"),
("Meucci invented the telephone",1871,"1850s–1870s","USA","Americas","Partly true","Antonio Meucci invented the telephone before Bell.","Meucci demonstrated voice transmission and filed a caveat in 1871 but couldn't afford to renew it. In 2002 the US House passed a resolution honouring him. Historians agree Bell's patent was decisive but credit Meucci's early work.","US House Resolution 269 (2002).","Antonio_Meucci"),
("Moon landing hoax",1969,"1969–1972","USA","Global","Debunked","The Apollo Moon landings were faked in a studio.","Six missions landed 12 astronauts. Retroreflectors left on the Moon are still used by observatories; 382 kg of Moon rocks are studied worldwide; the Soviet Union, which tracked the missions, never disputed them; and lunar orbiters (including India's Chandrayaan-2) have photographed landing sites.","Independent tracking, samples and photographs.","Moon_landing_conspiracy_theories"),
("Ancient aliens built the pyramids",-2560,"claims since 1960s","Egypt","Africa","Debunked","Aliens or a lost civilisation built the pyramids.","Archaeologists found workers' villages, bakeries and cemeteries at Giza, tools, quarries, and the Wadi al-Jarf papyri — the diary of an official named Merer — describing transporting limestone for the Great Pyramid. Such claims often dismiss the achievements of non-European peoples.","Excavations by Mark Lehner and Zahi Hawass; Wadi al-Jarf papyri.","Ancient_astronauts"),
("Area 51 and Roswell",1947,"1947 onwards","USA","Americas","Partly true","The US government hides crashed alien spacecraft.","In 1947 debris found near Roswell came from Project Mogul, a top-secret balloon programme to detect Soviet nuclear tests. Area 51 is real and was acknowledged by the CIA in 2013 as a test site for the U-2 and other spy planes, explaining UFO sightings. There is no evidence of aliens.","US Air Force reports (1994–97); declassified CIA history (2013).","Roswell_incident"),
("Donation of Constantine",800,"8th century; exposed 1440","Rome","Europe","Proven forgery","Emperor Constantine gave the Pope authority over the western Roman Empire.","Popes used this document to claim political power for centuries. In 1440 Italian scholar Lorenzo Valla proved it a forgery from the 8th century by its anachronistic Latin.","Lorenzo Valla's analysis.","Donation_of_Constantine"),
("Protocols of the Elders of Zion",1903,"1903","Russian Empire","Europe","Proven forgery","A secret Jewish plan for world domination.","The text was fabricated by the Russian secret police, partly plagiarised from an 1864 French satire about Napoleon III. The Times exposed it in 1921, but Henry Ford and the Nazis spread it, fuelling antisemitism and the Holocaust.","Philip Graves's exposé in The Times (1921); Bern trial (1935).","The_Protocols_of_the_Elders_of_Zion"),
("Piltdown Man",1912,"1912–1953","England","Europe","Proven hoax","A 'missing link' fossil found in England.","The skull was a human cranium combined with an orangutan jaw stained to look old. It misled science for 40 years until exposed in 1953.","Fluorine dating and examination (1953).","Piltdown_Man"),
("Titanic insurance switch",1912,"1912","Atlantic","Global","Debunked","The Titanic was swapped with its damaged sister ship Olympic for insurance fraud.","The wreck carries Titanic's hull number 401 in its propeller; the ship was underinsured; and the theory has no documentary support.","Wreck surveys since 1985.","Titanic_alternative_theories"),
("Nalanda library burned for months",1193,"c. 1193","Bihar","South Asia","Partly true","The Nalanda library burned for three months.","Nalanda was attacked around 1193 by Bakhtiyar Khalji's forces, as Minhaj-i-Siraj records. The detail of the library burning for months comes from a later Tibetan account, and some historians argue Nalanda continued in reduced form for decades.","Tabaqat-i-Nasiri; Tibetan sources.","Nalanda_mahavihara"),
("Kohinoor's curse and journey",1739,"1739–1849","India","South Asia","Documented journey (curse is myth)","The Kohinoor diamond was taken from India and brings misfortune to male owners.","The diamond passed from the Kakatiyas (traditionally) to the Delhi Sultanate, Mughals, Nadir Shah (1739), Afghan rulers, Ranjit Singh, and was taken by the British East India Company in 1849 from 10-year-old Duleep Singh. It is in the British Crown Jewels; India, Pakistan, Afghanistan and Iran have claimed it. The 'curse' is legend.","Dalrymple and Anand, Koh-i-Noor (2017).","Koh-i-Noor"),
("Hiroshima bombing was unnecessary",1945,"1945","Japan","East Asia","Disputed","The atomic bombs were not needed to end the war.","The US Strategic Bombing Survey (1946) concluded Japan would likely have surrendered by late 1945 without the bombs or invasion; others argue the bombs and Soviet entry shocked Japan's leaders into surrender. Some historians argue impressing the USSR was a motive.","US Strategic Bombing Survey; historians Gar Alperovitz, Tsuyoshi Hasegawa.","Debate_over_the_atomic_bombings_of_Hiroshima_and_Nagasaki"),
("Atlantis",-360,"Plato, c. 360 BCE","Mediterranean","Global","Myth","A lost advanced civilisation sank beneath the sea.","Atlantis first appears in Plato's dialogues Timaeus and Critias as a moral allegory. There is no archaeological evidence; some suggest the Thera eruption and Minoan Crete inspired it.","Plato's texts; archaeology.","Atlantis"),
("Gandhi's assassination plot warnings",1948,"January 1948","Delhi","South Asia","Documented fact","Authorities ignored warnings before Gandhi's assassination.","On 20 January 1948 Madanlal Pahwa set off a bomb at Birla House as part of the same conspiracy; police knew of the group but failed to stop Godse ten days later. The Kapur Commission (1969) criticised police failures.","Kapur Commission report.","Assassination_of_Mahatma_Gandhi"),
("Lavender scare",1950,"1950s","USA","Americas","Documented fact","The US government purged thousands of gay employees.","During the McCarthy era, thousands of gay and lesbian federal employees were fired as 'security risks'. The US apologised in 2017 (State Department).","Government records.","Lavender_scare"),
("Bhopal cover-up",1984,"1984 onwards","Bhopal, India","South Asia","Documented fact","Union Carbide ignored safety warnings and its chairman escaped trial.","Safety systems were off or broken; earlier leaks had been reported. Chairman Warren Anderson was arrested, released on bail, flew out of India and never returned. A 1989 settlement of $470 million was criticised as too low.","Court records; investigations.","Bhopal_disaster"),
]
